{{!-- The one way this site reports what just happened. Takes the message and
    its tone, and renders the treatment and the aria role the view-layer rule
    fixes for that tone: green where the act happened, neutral where nothing
    needed changing, red where it was refused. A notice with no tone reports no
    outcome and reads neutral.

    The message comes in one of three shapes. `text` is one sentence. `lines`
    is several sentences, one paragraph each, for a form refused on more than
    one field. A block call carries a message that needs markup of its own, a
    link or a code span, which an escaped sentence cannot hold:
    `{{#> outcome-notice tone='ok'}}...{{/outcome-notice}}`. The tone picks the
    treatment in every shape, so no caller ever writes the classes itself. --}}
{{#if text}}
  {{#if (eq tone 'ok')}}
    <div class="form-success-banner" role="status">{{text}}</div>
  {{else if (eq tone 'no')}}
    <div class="form-error-banner" role="alert">{{text}}</div>
  {{else}}
    <p class="form-notice" role="status">{{text}}</p>
  {{/if}}
{{else if (or lines.length @partial-block)}}
  {{#if (eq tone 'ok')}}
    <div class="form-success-banner" role="status">
  {{else if (eq tone 'no')}}
    <div class="form-error-banner" role="alert">
  {{else}}
    <div class="form-notice" role="status">
  {{/if}}
  {{#each lines}}<p>{{this}}</p>{{/each}}
  {{#if @partial-block}}{{> @partial-block}}{{/if}}
    </div>
{{/if}}
